    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF DCF, component build, 10-year horizon. Routed via dcf-methods SKILL.md: Cintas is a US operating company (uniform rental/facility services 76% of revenue, first aid & safety 13%, fire protection & other 11%) with conventional FCF; no bank/REIT/holdco characteristics, no dual currency, SBC is material (US market) so house and street bases diverge. No memory entry existed (first valuation). EBITDA margin driver is PRE-SBC: FY2026 GAAP operating income $2,606.5M + D&A $512.8M + SBC $128.1M + UniFirst transaction costs $15.1M = $3,262.5M = 29.0% of revenue; the engine then deducts SBC+withholding taxes via sbc_pct_path. D&A includes ~1.7% of revenue of intangible and capitalized-contract-cost amortization; commission cash is captured in the working-capital drag. Working capital: FY2024-26 cash WC absorbed ~29% of each revenue-dollar of growth (rental items in service, receivables, capitalized contract costs; FY26 -46%); wc_capture -35% used. Interest income ($5.1M FY2026) not stripped: net debt, not net cash. Buybacks: $952.1M FY2026 total repurchases of which $174.3M were withholding taxes (already in the SBC charge) and $777.8M open-market; the flat count is being funded (diluted count fell 413.5M FY24 -> 404.3M Q1 FY27). UNIFIRST: merger agreed 2026-03-10 ($155 cash + 0.7720 CTAS shares per UNF share, ~US$5.5bn), UNF holders approved 2026-06-12, FTC review ongoing, close expected before end CY2026, $350M reverse termination fee. Valued STANDALONE, matching management's standalone FY2027 guidance; at a fair price the deal is value-neutral before synergies, so the standalone value is the right anchor and synergies are an upside not in any scenario. Revisit on close: add issued shares, deal debt and UNF flows together.",
